Description: settings and onboarding for Myna dictation
 Myna Settings is the desktop application that sets up and configures Myna,
 the local speech-to-text dictation service shipped as the myna snap. It
 installs the myna snap and a speech backend snap, connects them, binds the
 dictation shortcut, and exposes the dictation settings (streaming mode,
 language, HUD style) that the daemon reads live.
 .
 It runs unconfined on the host because it drives snapd and runs snap
 commands as root through polkit, which a confined snap cannot do. The
 GSettings schema the daemon and this application share is installed by this
 package.
